  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy)\n(section) R.C. 3509.032(A)(1)-(2) (new section; alternative ID for absentee voters)\n(quote) (A) An elector to whom any of the following apply may cast absent voter's ballots by mail at an election by providing alternative identification instead of a copy of the elector's photo identification, in accordance with this section: (1) The elector is a uniformed services voter or overseas voter. (2) The elector does not have photo identification because the elector has a sincere religious objection to being photographed.\n(section) R.C. 3509.032(A)(3)\n(quote) (3) The elector does not have photo identification or cannot provide a copy of the elector's photo identification for any of the following reasons: (a) Because of the elector's severe medical condition; (b) Because of the elector's physical disability or infirmity; (c) Because of the elector's confinement in a jail or workhouse under sentence for a misdemeanor or awaiting trial on a felony or misdemeanor; (d) Because the elector lacks the mobility to obtain photo identification or a copy of the elector's photo identification; (e) Because of another material obstacle that makes the elector unable to obtain photo identification or a copy of the elector's photo identification, as described by the elector on the affirmation under division (B) of this section.\n(section) R.C. 4507.50(E)(3) (free state ID card for people experiencing homelessness)\n(quote) (3) The person is an individual experiencing homelessness who has not received such a fee waiver in the preceding twelve months.\n(section) R.C. 3509.11 (new section; free copy of photo ID)\n(quote) Upon request made in person by an elector, all of the following shall provide to the elector, without charge, a copy of the elector's photo identification for the purpose of casting absent voter's ballots by mail: (A) The secretary of state; (B) A board of elections; (C) The registrar of motor vehicles; (D) A public library.\n(c_mail_ballot_id)\n(section) R.C. 3509.03(B)(5)(a)-(b)\n(quote) (5) One of the following forms of identification: (a) A copy of the elector's photo identification enclosed with the application or an indication that the elector showed photo identification to the election officials when submitting the application in person, as permitted under division (C) of this section; (b) Except as otherwise permitted under section 3509.032 of the Revised Code, if the elector cannot provide photo identification at the time of applying for absent voter's ballots, the elector's Ohio driver's license or state identification card number or the last four digits of the elector's social security number.\n(section) R.C. 3509.03(C)\n(quote) (C) An elector who personally delivers the elector's application for absent voter's ballots to the board of elections may show the elector's photo identification to the election officials at that time instead of including a copy of the elector's photo identification with the application. The election officials shall mark the application to indicate that the elector has fulfilled the photo identification requirement to cast absent voter's ballots.\n(section) R.C. 3509.05(B)(1)\n(quote) (B)(1) Except as otherwise provided in divisions (B)(2) and (3) of this section, the elector shall provide one of the following: (a) The elector's Ohio driver's license or state identification card number on the statement of voter on the identification envelope; (b) The last four digits of the elector's social security number on the statement of voter on the identification envelope; (c) A copy of the elector's photo identification in the return envelope with the identification envelope. If the elector personally delivers the elector's voted ballots to the board of elections, the elector instead may show photo identification to the election officials at that time.\n(section) R.C. 3509.05(B)(2)\n(quote) (2) Except as otherwise provided in division (B)(3) of this section, if the elector did not provide photo identification when applying to cast absent voter's ballots, the elector shall do one of the following: (a) Enclose a copy of the elector's photo identification in the return envelope with the identification envelope; (b) Personally deliver the elector's voted ballots to the board of elections and show the election officials photo identification at that time.\n(section) R.C. 3509.031(C) (online portal)\n(quote) (C) The portal shall require the applicant to provide two forms of identification by complying with division (C)(1), (2), or (3) of this section, as applicable.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) R.C. 3509.031(A) (new section)\n(quote) (A) The secretary of state shall establish and maintain a secure online portal through which an elector may submit an application for absent voter's ballots, beginning with applications submitted on or after September 3, 2027, to cast absent voter's ballots in the general election held on November 2, 2027.\n(section) R.C. 3375.011(C) (library copy of photo ID)\n(quote) (C) Upon request by an elector, any library organized under Chapter 3375. of the Revised Code shall provide free of charge to the elector a copy of the elector's photo identification for the purpose of casting absent voter's ballots by mail.\n(other) 9.011 (new): homeless shelters and case-management agencies may keep copies of a person's Social Security card and birth records.\n(other) 2101.16, 2101.166 (new): probate court fee waiver for a marriage abstract for people experiencing homelessness.\n(other) 2303.20, 2303.202 (new): clerk of courts fee waiver for a name-change record or divorce/dissolution certificate for people experiencing homelessness.\n(other) 3109.14, 3705.24, 3705.242, 3705.243 (new), 3705.50 (new): fee waiver for birth certificates for people experiencing homelessness; health director collects and reports counts.\n(other) 4507.01, 4507.50-4507.52: state ID card fee waiver for people experiencing homelessness (with verification from a listed agency or school official); annual reports.\n(other) 3375.011: libraries give a free photocopy of a driver's license, permit or state ID card.\n(other) 3501.01: adds definitions of overseas voter, uniformed services and uniformed services voter.\n(other) 3503.02, 3503.13, 3503.153, 3503.16, 3509.07, 3509.08, 3509.10, 3511.01 (renumbered from 3511.011), 3511.02, 3511.021: uniformed-and-overseas voter application rules reorganised; federal post card application allowed; portal added; alternative ID allowed.\n(other) 3509.04, 3509.06: envelope statement and ballot-completeness rules updated for photo ID and affirmation.\n(other) 111.31, 3333.31, 3505.19: cross-reference or small wording changes (3505.19 religious-objection affidavit now also usable for absentee ballots).\n(other) version: 00_IN: no voting ID text; only fee waivers for a state ID card or birth certificate for people experiencing homelessness.\n(other) version: 01_RH: still no voting ID text; adds court-record fee waivers, shelter document storage (9.011) and more ID-card changes.\n(other) version: 02_PH: same as 01_RH (no voting ID text).\n(other) version: 03_RS: Senate substitute adds photo ID for absentee ballots (3509.03, 3509.05), online application portal (3509.031), alternative-ID affirmation (3509.032), free copies of photo ID (3509.11, 3375.011), and uniformed-and-overseas voter changes.\n(other) version: 04_PS, 05_CH, 06_EN: same voting ID text as 03_RS.\n(other) note: Slot quotes from amended sections are the resulting words (struck words removed, unchanged words kept). Title says it requires photo ID for absentee ballots. Slot a: the bill does not amend the in-person ID rule (3505.18); the existing rule is not reprinted. Action list shows \"Veto receipt\" on 2026-06-25 after enrollment; the saved data does not show whether the veto was overridden. House passage (2026-02-18) was on the House committee version (01_RH), which has no voting ID text.",
